{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]When [Cm]Athaliah saw her son was dead
She [Bb]rose up [Cm]to destroy the royal line
The whole [Bb]royal fami[Cm]ly fell [Abmaj7]under her hand
Seek[Bb]ing power, she did not spare [Cm]a single son
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But Jehoshe[Bb]ba took the young [Cm]child [Abmaj7]away
She stole him from [Bb]among [Cm]the dying [Abmaj7]sons
She hid him and his nurse in [Bb]a bed[Cm]room
Out of [Abmaj7]Athaliah's [Bb]sight, safe from the [Cm]blade
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He remained hidden with her in the [Bb]house of the LORD
[Cm]For six long years while Atha[Bb]liah reigned
[Cm]Jehoia[Abmaj7]da the priest kept the secret [Bb]close
Pre[Cm]serving [Abmaj7]the seed of David [Bb]in the temple's shad[Cm]ow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But Jehosheba took the [Bb]young child away
[Cm]She [Abmaj7]stole him from among the [Bb]dying [Cm]sons
She [Abmaj7]hid him and his nurse in a bed[Bb]room
[Cm]Out of At[Abmaj7]haliah's sight, [Bb]safe from the [Cm]blade
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Abmaj7]The daughter of King [Bb]Joram, sis[Cm]ter of Ahaziah
[Abmaj7]Cried out for the child when death [Bb]surround[Cm]ed them all
In [Abmaj7]the house of God, [Bb]the lineage [Cm]was kept
From the [Abmaj7]wrath of the queen who [Bb]sought to rule a[Cm]lone
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The royal line was [Bb]saved by [Cm]her courage
David's throne re[Bb]mained for the coming [Cm]days
{end_of_verse}

